<title>FRANCE: Revised figures confirm French Q3 GDP rose 0.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Revised figures confirm French Q3 GDP rose 0.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics office INSEE gave the following gross domestic product data (base 1980, changes from previous quarters in percent except stocks variation, in billions of 1980 francs.)</p>
<p>					 Q3	 Q2</p>
<p> Total GDP			   0.9     -0.2</p>
<p> Imports			     2.0     -0.5</p>
<p> Exports			     3.1     -1.8</p>
<p> Household consumption	   0.9	0.9</p>
<p> Investment			  0.9     -0.4</p>
<p> Stocks variation		 -4.2     -1.6</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following more detailed breakdown:</p>
<p>				Q3 96  Q2 96  Q1 96  Q4 95  Q3 95   1995</p>
<p> Total GDP		   0.9   -0.2     1.2  -0.5    0.2     2.2</p>
<p> Imports		     2.0   -0.5     2.1  -2.0    0.6     5.3</p>
<p> Exports		     3.1   -1.8     4.1  -0.6   -1.7     6.0</p>
<p> Household consumption   0.9    0.9     2.5  -0.3    0.0     1.8</p>
<p> Public consumption	0.4    0.6     0.4   0.3    0.4     0.9</p>
<p> Investment		  0.9   -0.4    -0.4  -0.3    1.5     2.6</p>
<p>  - business investment  3.0   -1.0     0.3  -1.3    1.3     3.8</p>
<p>  - household investment-3.1    1.8    -0.8   0.7    1.6     3.0</p>
<p>  - public investment    0.0   -2.0    -3.1   0.7    1.7    13.6</p>
<p> Stocks variation	 -4.2   -1.6    -8.2  -0.1    6.6    13.6</p>
<p> Internal demand	   0.5    0.2     0.7  -1.1    0.9     2.0</p>
<p>INSEE noted that so-called &quot;acquired growth&quot; for 1996 -- the annual growth that would be recorded if there were no change in the growth rate for the rest of the year -- was 1.3 percent.</p>
</text>
